# Review routing. GitHub requests a review from the owners of every path a pull
# request touches, and for each file it uses the LAST line that matches, so lines
# run from general to specific. Owners are the four maintainers in CONTRIBUTORS.md,
# by GitHub login, so keep the two in step. GitHub ignores an owner without write
# access to the repository, so each login needs it.
#
# Each area below has an owner (first login) and a backup (second login). The
# branch protection on main requires, for every file changed, an approval from one
# of that file's owners. The intended setup is two approvals, at least one of them
# from an owner of the area; the second approval becomes required once the branch
# protection setting is changed, separately from this file.

# Everything else: docs, ADRs, tests, scripts
